{
 "name": "heat_pressure_turbine_gate",
 "description": "33x6 AND-gated turbine intake: a HEAC heat rail over five stages, each stage = PSNS (pressure threshold 2/4/6/8/10) + TSNS (200/275/375/500/650 C) feeding a PSCN/NSCN pair and a SWCH, INSL-separated, on a CRMC/TTAN base.",
 "why": "Save 2396223 (description: the turbine requires heat and pressure): PSNS sparks when cell pressure exceeds its own temperature value (2,4,6,8,10) and TSNS when temperature exceeds its temperature (473..923K), so each SWCH only latches once both ladders have climbed past that stage -- a rising 5-step interlock. PSNS/TSNS thresholds are stored as temp_c exactly as captured (TSNS tmp2=2 kept). Deviation: the HEAC rail's top face is jacketed with INSL (lint heat_source_uninsulated); its bottom face must touch the sensors.",
 "source": "save 2396223, x356-388 y252-257; PSNS x=358,364,370,376,382 y=253; TSNS x=360,366,372,378,384 y=253; SWCH x=360..384 y=256",
